# Additional symbols to hide from the kernel dylib's exports, appended to Apple's
# xnu/tests/unit/tools/xnu_lib.unexport by harness/build.sh.
#
# XNU defines these BSD syscalls, and the dylib exporting them shadows libc for the test
# executables, so a plain read() in a runner lands in the kernel's read() and crashes. Apple's list
# already hides _open and _write for the same reason; these are the ones the harness needs on top.
# Hiding a symbol only removes it from the dylib's export table - kernel code inside the dylib still
# resolves it normally.
_read
_close
_lseek
